      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was wondering if this was possible. Many games offer an option to disable the desktop mirror window, so people who want to use it (as I do for recording) can keep it, while people who don't want it can disable it at will.\n\nI guess that maybe disabling it would interfere with the streaming camera, but it makes sense to also disable the streaming camera for those not interested in recording.\n\nIn my case, my major concern is that I usually leave my computer unattended in a different room, as I use the VR headset from the living room sofa, and that means my credentials (login and password) are easily visible for anyone (family or friends, specially kids) who might be around the computer room while I log in.... And also that I don't want my family to see what I am doing, don't want to have to do that much explaining XD\n\n(And before anyone complains about \"being a degenerate\", I already had to explain an \"I Am Cat\" play session, not again, thank you)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
